// Project: ifcJSON-based digital twin platform. Type: layer architecture, read left to right as in the paper's Fig. 1.
// Idea, ICCCBE 2024 section 3: the framework aims to "1) offer multiple wireless protocol options for constrained devices ...,
// 2) improve the data processing efficiency of BIM models on the web by adopting ifcJSON format, and 3) enhance the
// semantic representation of BIM models by integrating linked data in ifcJSON format with existing ontologies."
// Labels and sources (ICCCBE 2024, full paper):
//   Sensor, Network, Middleware, Application   Fig. 1 and the abstract (section 3's text says "data layer" for the third)
//   Wi-Fi, BLE, Zigbee, Z-Wave, LoRaWAN         3.2: "transmit sensor data to a gateway using WiFi, BLE, Zigbee, Z-wave, or
//                                                LoRaWAN protocols"; Fig. 1 gateways (no count drawn: 3.2 says six protocols
//                                                are considered, Fig. 1 draws five gateways)
//   Node-RED server                             Fig. 1: "Node-RED-based Server"
//   MQTT broker                                 3.3: "integrating the server system with an MQTT broker"
//   ifcJSON, linked data                        3.3: "a linked data version of an ifcJSON-based BIM model" (inside the server,
//                                                as in Fig. 1)
//   Brick, ifcOWL                               abstract: "ontologies, such as Brick ontology and ifcOWL"
//   browsers                                    Fig. 1: "Client Web Browser"
// Illustrative: one sensor glyph per gateway (Fig. 1 draws several). Not drawn: the NoSQL database and the BAS (3.3).
// Fine-line drawing (classes .dgf in global.css), in the 300 x 356 frame shared by the four project drawings.
